  "notes": "v238 — NAV-LANE-INFO-REAL (owner, Fri Oct 23, 2026 11:36 MDT, drive video + Rand McNally screenshots the benchmark): the turn pop-up showed NO lane information — it must show REAL lane guidance, arrows over the actual lanes for the upcoming turn, designed-in. The routing response carries no lane data (verified live Oct 21; BUGS.md), so the real source is OpenStreetMap turn:lanes — the marked movement(s) of EACH lane on the approach road — read by the same lazy Overpass lookup that already fetched the lane count (query widened to turn:lanes ways; same approach point 40m before the turn, same mirror fallback, same never-cache-a-failure discipline). The pop-up now paints through laneGuidanceHtml: when marked lanes exist, one cell per REAL lane shows the arrow(s) that lane actually allows and the lanes serving the maneuver burn bright (Rand McNally style); when no lane serves the move, none is lit — the tagging is shown, never faked. ORIENTATION RULE (named): only turn:lanes:forward on a one-way approach (or a motorway) is read — there the forward lanes are exactly the driver lanes in travel order; two-way combined tagging, ambiguity, junk tokens, or a count contradicting lanes:forward all answer nothing, and the card falls back to the shipped v196 count strip, or to no strip. No lane is ever invented. REPRODUCTION-FIRST: new tools/nav-lane-info-v238-test.js — all 7 wiring checks RED on the shipped code (no reader, no query, geometry-guess paint), 34/34 GREEN after. The v196 suite keeps every pure-function pin; its two wiring pins moved with the code under a supersede note and its named turn:lanes limitation is lifted. REGRESSIONS: nav-lanes 30/30, nav-inset 19/19, nav-popup 20/20, nav-cutoff 14/14, drive-surface 31/31, nav-tile-coverage 5/5, navigator 178/180 — all identical to baseline. Standing pin move 237 -> 238. Native unchanged (v42 OTA pointer; no new APK). Machine-green is preparation — the verdict is his next real drive.",
